OTEIN - 100 CALORIES - 3G SUGAR - 6G CARBS"},{"type":"General: Product/Version Code","notes":"CODE 350977 KMG"},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"Calories: 2000 2500\nTotal Fat Less than 65g 80g\nSat. Fat Less than 20g 25g\nCholesterol Less than 300mg 300mg\nSodium Less than 2400mg 2400mg\nPotassium 3500mg 3500mg\nTotal Carbohydrate 300g 375g\nDietary Fiber 25g 30g\nCalories per gram: \nFat 9 - Carbohydrate 4 - Protein 4\n"},{"type":"Formula re: Contains","notes":"CONTAINS: Egg, Milk, and Soybeans."},{"type":"Precautions re: Allergies","notes":"CONTAINS: Egg, Milk, and Soybeans."},{"type":"Precautions re: All Other","notes":"NOTICE: Use this product as a food supplement only. Do not use for weight reduction."},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"Significant product settling may occur."},{"type":"Storage","notes":"Store in a cool, dry place."},{"type":"Formula re: Contains","notes":"THE BENEFITS OF PROTEIN\nGNC Pro Performance(R) Whey Protein Complex combines protein from whey, soy, caseinate and egg to provide you with a full spectrum of amino acids."},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"Protein serves as a dietary source of amino acids. The body needs amino acids to build the various proteins used in the growth, repair and maintenance of body tissues such as skin, bones and muscles. More specifically, it supplies branched chain amino acids (BCAA) to athletes. BCAA are essential amino acids, which are part of muscle protein. They may preserve muscle glycogen stores and help reduce the amount of protein breakdown during exercise."},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"Protein Consumption \nDepending on your athletic goals, your protein requirements can vary. Serious athletes should consume approximately one gram of protein per pound of body weight. This should be spread over four to six small meals. Inadequate protein in your diet can limit muscle protein synthesis which can compromise your athletic goals. The amino acids from whey protein move quickly through the digestive system. The consumption of these proteins will result in a rapid rise in blood amino acids and stimulate protein synthesis."},{"type":"Suggested/Recommended/Usage/Directions","notes":"Whey Protein Complex can be taken immediately before and/or after your workout to support muscle protein synthesis."},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"TYPICAL NATURALLY OCCURRING AMINO ACID PROFILE PER SERVING: \nAlanine 717 mg \nArginine 898 mg \nAspartate 1917 mg \nCystine 278 mg \nGlutamine 3098 mg \nGlycine 507 mg \nHistidine 395 mg \nIsoleucine^ 893 mg \nLeucine^ 1546 mg \nLysine 1259 mg \nMethionine 298 mg \nPhenylalanine 737 mg \nProline 912 mg \nSerine 907 mg \nThreonine 912 mg \nTryptophan 278 mg \nTyrosine 580 mg \nValine^ 868 mg \nTotal 17000 mg\n^Indicates Branched Chain Amino Acid (BCAA) \n*When used in conjunction with an exercise program, this product provides essential building blocks for muscle recovery and growth."},{"type":"Suggested/Recommended/Usage/Directions","notes":"STACK WITH: GNC Pro Performance(R) RapidDrive(R) Arginine 5000(TM) and Creatine Monohydrate 5000."},{"type":"Seals/Symbols","notes":"{QRC} SCAN & LEARN MORE"},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"FULL SPECTRUM PROTEIN MIX"}],"targetGroups":["Adult (18 - 50 Years)"],"thumbnail":"","upcSku":"0 48107 08244 4","userGroups":[{"dailyValueTargetGroupName":"Adults and children 4 or more years of age","langualCode":"P0250","langualCodeDescription":"Adults and Children 4 years and above"}],"_source":"api"}